# This repo intentionally publishes only Dashboard/ -- everything else
# (raw/engineered data, trained models, pipeline scripts, notebooks) stays
# local. Some of it is 100MB+ (e.g. File/models/) and would fail a GitHub
# push outright; the rest is working data, not the public deliverable.
/File/
/Program/
/Doc/
*.ipynb
.ipynb_checkpoints/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.claude/

# The model-performance / methodology dashboard stays local only, never published.
# Globbed rather than listed file-by-file (2026-07-27): dashboard objects now live in
# per-version folders (Dashboard/fpl_v4/fpl_model_combined_v4.html), so the old
# explicit paths silently stopped matching and would have published it on the next push.
Dashboard/**/fpl_model_combined_*.html
Dashboard/**/fpl_model_combined_*.json
Dashboard/**/fpl_model_dashboard*.html
# The version history page is internal engineering detail -- leaks, bugs, negative
# results, per-experiment deltas -- not public-facing content for an FPL audience,
# so it follows the model dashboard and stays local. Delete these two lines if you
# want it published.
Dashboard/versions.html
Dashboard/versions.json
index.html

# Superseded dashboard versions and the pre-v2 archive stay local -- only the
# CURRENT version is published. They are large, and the version history page that
# indexes them is itself local-only (see above).
Dashboard/fpl_v2/
Dashboard/fpl_v3/
Dashboard/fpl_v4/
Dashboard/Archive/

# Only the deployed page (git.html at the repo root) and the data it fetches are
# published. The version folder's own HTML copies -- both combined dashboards and
# its record of the served git.html -- are local build inputs and references, not
# things the live site serves.
Dashboard/fpl_v5/*.html

# Review artefacts for the v5 mobile layout: full copies of the page with the
# proposed CSS, plus the iframe harness used to check it at true phone widths.
mockup_*.html
frame_test.html
